== Complete inputs from a new collector orbit
All ten points were fixed before section evaluation. Native precision-17 jets
pass five source equations, eight units/inverses, all thirteen descent
conjugates and a corrupted top-nu control. All 68 original/descended sections
agree; 196/324 products are evaluated. All 588 old F32 reference rows match.
Evaluation ranks are 68/196/324 in 2210 binary coordinates, not relation ranks.

Each effective divisor is 23Q+Pi, degree 115+13=128. Every one of ten
condition matrices has rank 128 and complete small/large kernels 68/196.
All thick-Q conditions, residue coordinates, kernel recombinations and
full precision-154 global vectors are checked and retained. Completeness
uses the existing genus-61 proper/pole/RR bridge, not rank alone.

== Signed class and exact isolation outcomes
The actual ten-step deck order is checked up to coefficient Frobenius.
Mixed weights are (4,1,-1,1,-1,-4,-1,1,-1,1). Positive-minus-negative and
paired-difference computations agree. Both signed zero tests have witness
dimension zero. Every quotient uses all generators; every product has an
independent arithmetic check.

The new F and 61F are nonprincipal. The isolated class 3721F is nonprincipal,
while 11 times and 121 times that class are principal. Direct 3721 and
successive 61,61 calculations agree. Thus the isolated source class has
exact order 11 under the retained Picard interpretation. The total order
of unisolated F was not determined, and the old order 671 was not assumed.

